IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mrca-member`

-- Guide to Determining Impairment and Compensation 2026 (MRCA s 67) -- Chapter 23: turning impairment points and a lifestyle
-- rating into the weekly amount of permanent impairment compensation, as a fraction of the s 74 maximum. Read from the
-- deposited Guide instead of asked as an input. A module beside mrca-member.l4; it computes the weekly amount that module's
-- lump-sum question takes as `my weekly amount`, and calls its rules without restating them.
--
-- SEAT: the current or former member, as in mrca-member.l4. "With these impairment points and this lifestyle rating, what
-- weekly amount does the Guide give me, and what share may I take as a lump sum?"
--
-- Edition: the Guide as made (register id F2026L00595, made 4 May 2026 by the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation
-- Commission under s 67(1); unamended, no compilation registered), deposited at
-- ../../../guide-to-determining-impairment-and-compensation-2026/registers/source-bundle/F2026L00595.txt (retrieved
-- 2026-10-23). Tables 23.1 (warlike and non-warlike service) and 23.2 (peacetime service) are at lines 11474 to 12900 of the
-- deposit, one cell per line; the two tables below were transcribed from those lines by script and checked: 77 rows each
-- (impairment 0 and 5 to 80), 8 lifestyle columns (0 to 7), every row and column non-decreasing. The weighted-average formula
-- for mixed service is an image in the authorised rendering, transcribed in F2026L00595.formulas.md beside the deposit.
--
-- IN: Chapter 23 (the compensation factors; mixed service). OUT: how impairment points are assessed (Chapters 1-21), the
-- Combined Values Chart (Chapter 18, asked as the combined rating C), the lifestyle rating (Chapter 22, asked as L), the lump
-- sum factors (Chapter 24, the Actuary's), Chapters 25 and 26 (old VEA and DRCA conditions). The s 74 maximum weekly amount is
-- indexed under s 404 and asked as an input (the Act's $233.07 before indexation; the Guide's examples use $245.82 and, at
-- 1 July 2024, $421.72).

§ `Guide to Determining Impairment and Compensation -- my weekly amount`

§§ `Chapter 23 -- Tables 23.1 and 23.2, the compensation factors`

-- "Table 1 is for warlike and non-warlike service. Table 2 is for peacetime service." "For impairment greater than 80 points,
-- the value is always 1.00." Each row: impairment points, then the factors for lifestyle ratings 0, 1, ..., 7.
