-- The service kinds are mrca-member.l4's `Kind of service`. s 67(2)(a) of the Act: different methods for "(i) service
-- injuries or diseases that relate to warlike service or non-warlike service; and (ii) other service injuries or diseases";
-- so British nuclear test defence service and hazardous service take Table 23.2 with peacetime service.
GIVEN `service` IS A `Kind of service`
      `impairment points` IS A NUMBER
      `lifestyle rating` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the compensation factor` MEANS
    IF `impairment points` GREATER THAN 80
    THEN JUST 1
    ELSE IF `lifestyle rating` LESS THAN 0 OR `lifestyle rating` GREATER THAN 7
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE CONSIDER lookup `impairment points` `the table`
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
              WHEN JUST row THEN JUST (at row `lifestyle rating`)
    WHERE
        `the table` MEANS
            IF `service` EQUALS `warlike service` OR `service` EQUALS `non-warlike service, including peacekeeping`
            THEN `Table 23.1`
            ELSE `Table 23.2`

@export What compensation factor does the Guide give for my impairment points and lifestyle rating (Chapter 23, Tables 23.1 and 23.2)?
GIVEN `service` IS A `Kind of service` @desc The kind of service the conditions relate to: warlike or non-warlike service (Table 23.1), or peacetime, hazardous or British nuclear test defence service (Table 23.2); for a mix of the two groups, use the mixed-service question
      `impairment points` IS A NUMBER @desc Your combined impairment rating under the Guide (Chapter 18), not rounded; 80 or more pays the maximum
      `lifestyle rating` IS A NUMBER @desc Your lifestyle rating under Chapter 22, a whole number from 0 to 7
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is my compensation factor` MEANS `the compensation factor` `service` `impairment points` `lifestyle rating`

-- "The maximum compensation is multiplied by the compensation factor to give the weekly amount of compensation payable."
@export What weekly amount of permanent impairment compensation does the Guide give me (s 74, Chapter 23)?
GIVEN `service` IS A `Kind of service` @desc The kind of service the conditions relate to (warlike or non-warlike: Table 23.1; any other: Table 23.2)
      `impairment points` IS A NUMBER @desc Your combined impairment rating under the Guide
      `lifestyle rating` IS A NUMBER @desc Your lifestyle rating, 0 to 7
      `the maximum weekly amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 74 maximum weekly amount in force, in dollars ($233.07 in the Act, indexed each 1 July under s 404)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What weekly amount does the Guide give me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the compensation factor` `service` `impairment points` `lifestyle rating`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST f THEN JUST (f TIMES `the maximum weekly amount`)

§§ `Chapter 23 -- mixed service`

-- "If the service-caused conditions lead to impairment ratings of A for warlike (or non-warlike) service and B for peacetime
-- service, then the compensation payable will be a weighted average"; formula (F2026L00595.formulas.md, image49):
-- CF final (C, L) = (A x CF wl (C, L) + B x CF pt (C, L)) / (A + B). "If a person has 2 or more conditions resulting from
-- warlike (or non-warlike) service, the impairment rating A is the sum of the impairment points for each of those conditions";
-- likewise B. The formula does not round; the Guide's Example 2 shows 0.380 for 0.3798 (NOTES.md finding 13).
GIVEN `warlike points A` IS A NUMBER
      `peacetime points B` IS A NUMBER
      `combined rating C` IS A NUMBER
      `lifestyle rating` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the mixed compensation factor` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the compensation factor` `warlike service` `combined rating C` `lifestyle rating`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST wl THEN
        CONSIDER `the compensation factor` `peacetime service` `combined rating C` `lifestyle rating`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST pt THEN JUST (((`warlike points A` TIMES wl) PLUS (`peacetime points B` TIMES pt)) DIVIDED BY (`warlike points A` PLUS `peacetime points B`))

@export I have conditions from both warlike (or non-warlike) and peacetime service. What weekly amount does the Guide give me (Chapter 23, combined ratings)?
GIVEN `warlike points A` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the impairment points of your conditions from warlike or non-warlike service
      `peacetime points B` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the impairment points of your conditions from peacetime service
      `combined rating C` IS A NUMBER @desc Your combined impairment rating for all the conditions (Chapter 18)
      `lifestyle rating` IS A NUMBER @desc Your lifestyle rating, 0 to 7
      `the maximum weekly amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 74 maximum weekly amount in force, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What weekly amount for mixed service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the mixed compensation factor` `warlike points A` `peacetime points B` `combined rating C` `lifestyle rating`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST f THEN JUST (f TIMES `the maximum weekly amount`)

§§ `s 78 -- the lump sum choice, on the Guide's weekly amount`

@export With the Guide's weekly amount, what share of my compensation may I convert to a lump sum (s 78(1))?
GIVEN `service` IS A `Kind of service` @desc The kind of service the conditions relate to (warlike or non-warlike: Table 23.1; any other: Table 23.2)
      `impairment points` IS A NUMBER @desc Your combined impairment rating under the Guide
      `lifestyle rating` IS A NUMBER @desc Your lifestyle rating, 0 to 7
      `the maximum weekly amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 74 maximum weekly amount in force, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF NUMBER)
`What share may I convert, on the Guide's amount` MEANS
    CONSIDER `What weekly amount does the Guide give me` `service` `impairment points` `lifestyle rating` `the maximum weekly amount`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST w THEN JUST (`What share may I convert to a lump sum` w `the maximum weekly amount`)
